      "sourceTextSha256": "cdb3dfcb37a46de9aa1d5d81eb723b6a679b89978f6a51c5053c9ed623130b9b",
      "text": "Day 2  ·  After breakfast, congress in the morning.\nAfter the congress, half-day excursion to Corcovado Mountain. From the station, the environmentally friendly train climbs through the jungle, with spectacular views of the Tijuca Forest, home to monkeys and other exotic animals and birds. At the top, 700 m above sea level, stands the symbol of Rio de Janeiro, the 38 m Statue of Christ the Redeemer, built in 1931, with breathtaking panoramas over the city, the Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, Maracanã stadium and Sugar Loaf. Lunch at Confeitaria Colombo.\nIn the evening, dinner at Rio Scenarium, famous for its dances and nightlife.",
      "provenance": {
